# Docs / markdown — ignore all except README, agent instructions, and
# app-rendered content. AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md are how the project is built;
# leaving them untracked meant every contributor started from scratch.
*.md
*.MD
!README.md
!AGENTS.md
!CLAUDE.md
# Licensing / project-level docs at the repo root belong in git and must be
# visible (a hidden LICENSING.md defeats the purpose).
!LICENSING.md
!CLA.md
!COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md
!REPOS.md
# Legal drafts (commercial licence agreement, etc.) belong in git.
!legal/
!legal/**/*.md
!resources/markdown/
!resources/markdown/**
# Plans are the record of what was built and why. Versioning them is the
# whole point — a plan marked DONE_ is history, not scratch.
!Documentation & Planning/
!Documentation & Planning/**

# The same for docs and changelogs. Written and then silently untracked —
# the Windows setup guide, the transfer instructions and two changelogs
# existed on one machine only, which is the opposite of what they are for.
!docs/
!docs/**/*.md
!changelog/
!changelog/**/*.md

# What one agent learned, for the next one. Same reason as the two above: it is
# written to be read by whoever comes next, which cannot happen if it lives on
# one machine.
!.claude/
!.claude/**/*.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Media — never commit the library
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Laravel's nested storage/.gitignore files already cover the default paths,
# but the library is the user's own films, music and books: a single misplaced
# folder pushed to a remote is expensive to undo and impossible to fully
# retract. These rules are deliberately redundant so that stays true even if a
# watch folder, an export, or a converted copy lands somewhere unexpected.

/storage/app/private/

# Database snapshots. These hold the whole catalogue — every title, every play,
# every profile — so committing one would publish the library.
/storage/backups/

# Published release bundles. Large binaries, rebuildable, and signed with a key
# that is deliberately not in this repository.
/storage/app/updates/
/storage/app/public/
/media/
/library/
/uploads/
/downloads/

# Anywhere a media folder might be created by hand or by config.
**/media/library/
**/media/unsorted/
**/media/converted/
**/media/subtitles/
**/media/book-assets/

# Media and subtitle files, wherever they appear.
*.mp3
*.flac
*.m4a
*.aac
*.wav
*.aiff
*.aif
*.ogg
*.oga
*.opus
*.wma
*.alac
*.ape
*.wv
